Root cause:
The bug was caused by a change in the way the tooltip string was constructed, specifically the order of operations in concatenating the `link` to the message before wrapping it in HTML. This led to incorrect tooltip formatting, resulting in not all warnings being displayed properly in the editor.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(message.startsWith("<html>") ? XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message): XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message)) + link ;
```
Reason:
The tooltip string was constructed by concatenating the `link` to the message before wrapping the entire string in HTML. This incorrect order of operations caused the tooltip formatting to be incorrect, leading to not all warnings being displayed properly in the editor.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml((message.startsWith("<html>") ? XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message): XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message)) + link);
```
Reason:
The fix changes the order of operations by wrapping the concatenated string (message + link) in HTML after ensuring the message is properly formatted. This ensures that the tooltip is correctly formatted, allowing all warnings to be displayed properly in the editor.


